# .protected.local — paths the AI must NOT touch (OPT-IN, gitignored).
#
# Copy this file to `.protected.local` to lock paths against AI edits. While
# `.protected.local` exists, the Claude Code / Cursor guard BLOCKS Edit/Write
# to any path listed below — and to `.protected.local` itself. To change what
# is protected, edit `.protected.local` by hand; the AI cannot. Delete the file
# to lift all restrictions.
#
# Notes
# - One repo-relative glob per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # ignored.
# - A bare directory matches everything beneath it. `*` matches within a path
#   segment; `**` matches across segments.
# - Convenience fence, not a security control: a human can edit or remove this
#   file. The hard guarantee is server-side branch protection.
#
# Suggested defaults — the security/config surface the AI should not edit
# (uncomment what you want to lock):
# .claude/
# .cursor/hooks/
# .cursor/hooks.json
# .github/workflows/
# .husky/
# CLAUDE.md
# SECURITY.md
